/*!
\page page_stv0vertex StV0Vertex

\brief Vertex representing a V0 neutral two-prong decay (K0s, Lambda, anti-Lambda, γ conversion).

\section stv0vertex_overview Overview
StV0Vertex stores the secondary decay vertex of a neutral particle into
two charged daughters.  It holds the 3-D decay position, daughter momenta
at the vertex, and DCA quantities needed for V0 selection.

V0 vertices are stored in StEvent::v0Vertices().

\section stv0vertex_hierarchy Class Hierarchy
\code{.cpp}
TObject → StObject → StMeasuredPoint → StVertex → StV0Vertex
\endcode

\section stv0vertex_datamembers Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| mDaughters | StPtrVecTrack | Non-owning: [0]=negative, [1]=positive daughter. |
| mDcaDaughtersToPrimaryVertex[2] | Float_t | DCA of each daughter to PV (cm). |
| mMomentumOfDaughters[2] | StThreeVectorF | Daughter momenta at vertex (GeV/c). |
| mDcaDaughters | Float_t | DCA between daughters at the decay point (cm). |
| mDcaParentToPrimaryVertex | Float_t | DCA of V0 to primary vertex (cm). |

\section stv0vertex_methods Key Methods

\code{.cpp}
const StSPtrVecV0Vertex& v0s = event->v0Vertices();
for (size_t i = 0; i < v0s.size(); ++i) {
    const StV0Vertex* v0 = v0s[i];
    if (v0->dcaDaughters() > 0.8) continue;
    const StThreeVectorF& pMinus = v0->momentumOfDaughter(negative);
    const StThreeVectorF& pPlus  = v0->momentumOfDaughter(positive);
    StThreeVectorF pV0 = v0->momentum();
    // compute invariant mass under K0s or Lambda hypothesis
}
\endcode

\sa \ref page_stvertex, \ref page_stxivertex
*/
